{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "C# Environment", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about C# environment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand important information about client software for the identity metasystem in spoken or written documents. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on principles, concepts, and features of general purpose computer programming languages.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le03ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Superlatives - Short Adjectives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<strong>Superlatives</strong> are the form of an adjective to indicate that the noun is on the top of a certain group with the characteristic that is mentioned.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The biggest advantage is portability.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The NET framework allows C# to operate smoothly with Windows; it's the best option available.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Generally, when the adjective has one syllable, we add <strong>_est</strong> to the adjective.  </br> <span class=\"italic\">Example: clean-cleanest </span> </br> </br> If there is a vowel followed by a consonant at the end of the adjective, we double the last consonant.  </br> <span class=\"italic\">Example: hot- hottest </span> </br> </br> If the adjective ends in <strong>\u2013y</strong>, we change it to <strong>i</strong>.  </br> <span class=\"italic\">e.g. happy- happiest</span> </br></br>  There are also some irregular adjectives. Even though they are one-syllable words, we don't add the suffix _est to make them superlative but use a fixed word that we must learn by heart. </br></br>  Examples: </br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Good\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Best\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Bad\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Worst\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Exceptions:</br> With these adjectives, you need to add<span class=\"strong\"> the most</span>: </br> Fun - the most fun (not funniest) </br> Real \u2013 the most real (not realest) </br> Right \u2013 the most right (not rightest) </br> Wrong \u2013 the most wrong (not wrongest) </span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Using Online Tools to Compile and Execute", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can find tools to compile and execute C# codes on the internet. They allow you work online instead of downloading specific programs or applications for this task.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Nowadays, you have some important resources on the internet to compile and execute C# language codes. You can access them through your favorite browser. </br></br>  You can go to your favorite search engine and type \u201conline compiler.\u201d When you tap the search button, several options of compiling and executing codes appear. You can choose any of them depending on your needs and the characteristics those web pages offer. </br></br>  Some of these pages give you the codes to compile, so, at the beginning, you only copy and paste those codes to come up with an idea of how the platforms work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "multi-platform ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "that works on two or more operating systems. ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This means that programmers can use any language and that you can run that code on any hardware on which .NET is supported, thanks to having multi-platform applications.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le03ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " runtime environment ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a tool included in some programming software that helps executing tests on the application being developed in real time ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Even though you find the word \"framework\" on this tool's name, it also provides the Common Language Runtime (CLR), which is a runtime environment that handles management, exceptions, and security. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le03ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "portability ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a characteristic of a program where the program can be used in different operating systems without major problems", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The biggest advantage is portability. This means that programmers can use any language and that you can run that code on any hardware on which .NET is supported, thanks to having multi-platform applications.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le03ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "run", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to execute a program", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It runs on the Windows operating system.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le03ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "uninstall ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to remove from your computer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On older versions of Windows, you have to uninstall and then reinstall a new version of .NET to get things working.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le03ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "reinstall ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to install it again", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On older versions of Windows, you have to uninstall and then reinstall a new version of .NET to get things working.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le03ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Browse the internet to find online tools to compile and execute programming code.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare three of the pages you found, mentioning the best, worst, biggest, etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your findings with a mate.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I can browse the internet to look for online compiling and executing tools for programming code", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can compare things by using the appropriate adjectives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can express my ideas by describing how things are in the moment and how to differentiate them.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can present basic information about the .NET framework.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about integrat